Package: strainselect
Title: Select Bacterial Strains to Sequence Based on Their Metadata
Version: 0.2.0
Authors@R: c(
    person("Marie", "Vallée", , "marie.vallee@anses.fr", role = "aut",
           comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0002-4233-8400")),
    person("Laurent", "Guillier", , "guillier.laurent@gmail.com", role = c("aut", "cre"),
           comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0002-7867-2937"))
  )
Description: Helps choosing which bacterial strains to sequence from a
    collection described by categorical metadata (sampling context, matrix,
    region, year...). Two methods are provided. The clustering method groups
    the strains into a chosen number of clusters using the Gower distance and
    hierarchical clustering, and selects the best clustered strain of each
    cluster according to its silhouette width; it is suited when the number
    of strains that can be sequenced is limited. The profile method groups
    the strains that share exactly the same metadata and selects one strain
    per group, so that every distinct profile is represented.
